stores snapshots and replays events; it does not reverse a real Python process."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":78,"data-source-end-line":78},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each recording should include revision, build settings, platform/architecture, program and inputs, JIT mode, and extraction method. Each artifact or event should have a stable ID, semantic kind, source span when available, relevant code/frame/executor identity, instruction or micro-op position, state change, and provenance. Label provenance as captured, derived, or explanatory. Do not fabricate a source span for a synthetic instruction."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":80,"data-source-end-line":80},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capture raw and optimized representations separately. Proposed event families include artifact creation, frame push/pop, instruction execution, reference/stack update, specialization, recording start/stop, executor installation/entry, side exit, deopt, invalidation, and exception. The final schema depends on what instrumentation can reliably expose; not all listed events are currently available as public hooks."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":82,"data-source-end-line":82},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Controls should include play/pause, step, back, reset, chapter selection, mode selection, speed, and an inspect panel. “Skip warmup” is an explicit timeline jump. Mode changes should restore the corresponding capture at a shared checkpoint or restart, rather than magically enabling JIT in the middle of a mismatched recording."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"evidence-and-validation-plan","data-source-start-line":84,"data-source-end-line":84},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evidence and validation plan"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":86,"data-source-end-line":86},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before drawing 3D, obtain a minimal set of artifacts and transitions from the pinned revision. Successful validation means correct semantics and provenance, not merely plausible animation."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":88,"data-source-end-line":88},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use AST, symbol-table, and disassembly facilities for externally inspectable compiler artifacts. CFG and preprocessing details may need internal test interfaces or dedicated extraction; do not imply ordinary "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"dis"}]},{"type":"text","value":" exposes the compiler's full CFG. For runtime bytecode use the appropriate adaptive/cache-aware disassembly and clearly separate it from original code-object output."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":90,"data-source-end-line":90},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"CPython's "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/036d309cf542986a39eeba5ca805b2ec7619731d/Tools/jit/example_trace_dump.py","className":["external-link"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"example_trace_dump.py"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","className":["external-link-icon"]},"children":[]}]},{"type":"text","value":" recommends a debug micro-op-interpreter build with stats to inspect trace structure. "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/036d309cf542986a39eeba5ca805b2ec7619731d/Modules/_opcode.c#L374","className":["external-link"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"_opcode.get_executor"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","className":["external-link-icon"]},"children":[]}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/036d309cf542986a39eeba5ca805b2ec7619731d/Lib/dis.py#L233","className":["external-link"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"dis.py"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","className":["external-link-icon"]},"children":[]}]},{"type":"text","value":" provide another inspection lead. These can validate trace concepts, but native execution and emitted machine code require a native-JIT build and its own evidence."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":92,"data-source-end-line":92},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Avoid relying on "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"sys.settrace"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to observe an otherwise unchanged JIT run: "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/036d309cf542986a39eeba5ca805b2ec7619731d/Python/ceval.c#L1090","className":["external-link"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"stop_tracing_and_jit"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","className":["external-link-icon"]},"children":[]}]},{"type":"text","value":" checks tracing/profiling state before optimization, and "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/036d309cf542986a39eeba5ca805b2ec7619731d/Python/bytecodes.c#L3550","className":["external-link"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"ENTER_EXECUTOR"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","className":["external-link-icon"]},"children":[]}]},{"type":"text","value":" can fall back for instrumentation. Assess capture perturbation explicitly. An opcode-step teaching trace and a native run may need separate captures linked at semantic checkpoints."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":94,"data-source-end-line":94},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate equal outputs and exceptions across modes; consistent stack effects and frame lifetimes; real specialization and executor installation; correct continuation after exits; and at least one evidenced optimization. Preserve raw diagnostic output alongside normalized fixtures. Do not claim a speedup from animation speed or debug-build timings."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":96,"data-source-end-line":96},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The next implementation milestone is a reproducible interpreter artifact bundle for one program plus a plain replay inspector and validated block routing. Then add a verified interpreter branch or guard-miss scenario, and only then use "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"/lat.md/scene"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"scene"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"className":["wiki-link-ref-count"],"ariaLabel":"5 references"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"5"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" to render the same state transitions spatially. JIT, full memory management, concurrency, generators, imports, and performance benchmarking are deferred. On-demand capture for small editable programs remains a feasibility direction, not an implemented capability."}]}]},"title":"Presentation approach","gitTree":null,"tableOfContents":[{"id":"presentation-approach","title":"Presentation approach","depth":1,"errorCount":0,"hasGitChanges":false},{"id":"one-world-with-two-execution-modes","title":"One world with two execution modes","depth":2,"errorCount":0,"hasGitChanges":false},{"id":"visual-entities-and-flows","title":"Visual entities and flows","depth":2,"errorCount":0,"hasGitChanges":false},{"id":"candidate-walkthroughs","titl